From eeec7b8eb95f7e9060897c43a6c382916e0a21ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "randomizedcoder dave.seddon.ca@gmail.com" <dave.seddon.ca@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 22:13:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ReportOutputs: fix buffer-size arg in (l4s) connection-report
 append

reporter_print_connection_report() builds the per-connection suffix line
in a fixed 512-byte `linebuffer`, advancing `b` after each snprintf and
passing the remaining space as `SNBUFFERSIZE - strlen(linebuffer)`. The
(l4s) branch instead passed `SNBUFFERSIZE - strlen(b)`. Once `b` has been
advanced by an earlier append (e.g. the UDP server "(seq no=N)" field),
strlen(b) is ~0, so the size argument (~512) exceeds the actual bytes
remaining at `b` (~498). The write itself (" (l4s)", 6 bytes) fits, but
under _FORTIFY_SOURCE=3 __snprintf_chk validates the size argument against
__builtin_dynamic_object_size(b) and aborts (SIGABRT) because size >
remaining object size. (At _FORTIFY_SOURCE<=2 the static object-size check
can't track the advanced pointer, so it silently no-ops -- the bug only
bites at level 3, which distros/NixOS now default to.)

Trigger: UDP datagrams sent to a --permit-key server without the key. Each
datagram produces a per-packet "permit key fail" connection report that
hits this path with L4S set, crashing the server.

Fix: use strlen(linebuffer), matching all 25 other appends in the function.

Reproduced on aarch64 (RPi4, NixOS, gcc 15.2, _FORTIFY_SOURCE=3) and on
x86_64 with -O2 -D_FORTIFY_SOURCE=3; server survives the same blast after
the fix.
---
 src/ReportOutputs.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ReportOutputs.c b/src/ReportOutputs.c
index 522699fe..bc61a58f 100644
--- a/src/ReportOutputs.c
+++ b/src/ReportOutputs.c
@@ -3257,7 +3257,7 @@ void reporter_print_connection_report(struct ConnectionInfo *report) {
         b += n;
     }
     if (isUDPL4S(report->common)) {
-        n = snprintf(b, SNBUFFERSIZE - strlen(b), " (l4s)");
+        n = snprintf(b, SNBUFFERSIZE - strlen(linebuffer), " (l4s)");
         FAIL_exit((n < 0), "fail append l4s");
         FAIL_exit((strlen(linebuffer) >= SNBUFFERSIZE), "buffer overflow l4s");
         b += n;
-- 
